  "name": {
    "en": "Chinatown (Yaowarat)"
  },
  "tagline": {
    "en": "Street food after dark, gold shops, old shophouses."
  },
  "about": {
    "en": "Yaowarat Road is the spine of Bangkok's Chinatown, with gold shops by day and street food stalls after dark. The MRT Blue line stops at Wat Mangkon and Hua Lamphong. Talat Noi, down by the river, is a maze of old shophouses, shrines and workshops that has become a cafe district; Song Wat Road along the river is older warehouses turning into bars and galleries. Hotels are small and characterful rather than large."
  },
